Not covered by the Apache License: code ported from AOHPAgentDriverApp
======================================================================

The files below were ported from the stock driver app of the Android Open
Harness Project, https://github.com/aohp-os/AOHPAgentDriverApp (package
org.aohp.agentdriver.executor), so that this app answers the same agent bridge
protocol. That repository states no licence. Its authors keep all rights in
their code, and nothing here grants any right to it. Each file says so in its
first lines.

  app/src/main/java/org/aohp/driver/bridge/ShellExecutor.java
  app/src/main/java/org/aohp/driver/bridge/AohpVdClient.java
  app/src/main/java/org/aohp/driver/bridge/AohpAgentViewClient.java
  app/src/main/java/org/aohp/driver/bridge/AohpEventStreamClient.java
  app/src/main/java/org/aohp/driver/bridge/AohpSecurityBridgeClient.java
  app/src/main/java/org/aohp/driver/bridge/CgroupUsage.java
      as upstream's, but for the package and import lines.
  app/src/main/java/org/aohp/driver/bridge/AohpContainerClient.java
  app/src/main/java/org/aohp/driver/bridge/BridgeWebSocketServer.java
  app/src/main/java/org/aohp/driver/bridge/JsonCommandHandler.java
      upstream's, with changes and additions made here since the port
      (commit b630bce, 2026-10-02; the history of each file shows them).

What was changed or added in those files in this repository is offered under
the Apache License 2.0, as far as it can be told apart from upstream's code.
A few lines elsewhere follow upstream's as well: the encrypted-preferences
setup in bridge/SecretStore.java, and declarations the bridge needs in
AndroidManifest.xml and res/xml/accessibility_service_config.xml.

An author of AOHPAgentDriverApp who wants this handled another way is asked to
open an issue on this repository.


